\tag{discrete}

\import{discrete-macros}

\taxon{Example}
\p{Is #{f : \Z \to \Z} defined by #{f(x) = 3x+2} invertible? No, although it is indeed one-to-one, it is not onto.  For example, there is no #{x \in \Z} such that #{f(x) = 6}; the output of #{f} will never be a multiple of #{3}.}


